<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>3.2.3: Writing Linear Models without Technology</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00717</md:content-id>
    <md:title>3.2.3: Writing Linear Models without Technology</md:title>
    <md:uuid>09f3ce5c-7bcc-43ff-b4e2-1511e0a8a105</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>Linear models can also be found by hand in some situations when the data follows a linear pattern since the slope remains the same between data points. </para>
<para><emphasis>Linear Models from Tables</emphasis></para>
<blockquote>
  <para>
  </para>
  <para>For 1 - 4, use the scenario and table below:</para>
  <para>The table below shows the number of songs Marcus will have in his collection as he adds new songs each month.</para>

<table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
  <thead>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Number of months, \(t\)</entry>
      <entry>0</entry>
      <entry>1</entry>
      <entry>2</entry>
      <entry>3</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Number of songs, \(N\)</entry>
      <entry>200</entry>
      <entry>215</entry>
      <entry>230</entry>
      <entry>245</entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>
</blockquote>

<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="f00e2119-ccd9-489c-9383-a06fc2430966" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0"><!--Q#1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="50701f9a-8db4-46eb-a7b0-673edcb2a852" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="200">
    <problem>
      <para> What is the initial amount of songs, or the \(y\)-intercept of this situation? </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 200</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q#2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="b76d8608-acae-4296-83b1-ea0609be1338" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="15">
    <problem>
      <para> What is the slope, or rate of change? </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 15</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </div>
</div>

<!--Q#3-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Write the equation of the linear model that represents the situation in slope-intercept form. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(N = 15t + 200\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="53b0d665-d880-493b-9cce-134ef1b35cc0" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0"><!--Q#4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="487937b8-cda6-4e24-836b-d9802cb72dac" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="320">
    <problem>
      <para> How many songs will Marcus have in 8 months? </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 320</para>
      <para> Compare your answer: 
        \(N = 15(8) + 200=320\)</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q#5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="c2dc9fc0-7c03-4b46-aa0b-09e5d9f9e26e" data-problem-comparator="float" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="12.5">
    <problem> 
      <blockquote>
        <para>For 5 - 8, use the situation and table below:</para>
        <para>A new plant food is introduced to a young tree to test its effect on the height of the tree. The table shows the height of the tree, H, in feet \(x\) months since measurements began.</para>
     
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
        <thead>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Number of months, \(x\)</entry>
            <entry>2</entry>
            <entry>4</entry>
            <entry>6</entry>
            <entry>8</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Height in feet, \(H\)</entry>
            <entry>13.5</entry>
            <entry>14.5</entry>
            <entry>15.5</entry>
            <entry>16.5</entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
        </blockquote>
      
      <para> What is the initial height of the tree, or the \(y\)-intercept, when measurements began? </para>
      <para>(Hint: Work each row backwards to where \(x= 0\).)</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q#6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="c61b5a88-59f5-463a-af77-a760b9dcdc31" data-problem-comparator="text" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="1/2">
    <problem>
      <para> What is the slope, or rate of change? </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here as a fraction in simplest form:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(\frac12\)</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </div>
</div>

<!--Q#7-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Write the equation of the linear model that represents the situation in slope-intercept form. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(H= \frac12 x\) +12.5\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="2b1801c5-96f3-43a5-97fe-3b8878ec8eec" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0"><!--Q#8-->
  <exercise data-content-id="2f1f631d-86fb-4a2c-bbb4-bf2eafd59a62" data-problem-comparator="float" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="19.5">
    <problem>
      <para> What will the height of the tree be in 14 months? </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 19.5</para>
      <para> Compare your answer: 
        \(H= \frac12 (14) +12.5 =19.5\)</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q#9-->
  <exercise data-content-id="10194ca5-8de5-4c66-80e3-516330af7969" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="30">
    <problem> 
      <para><emphasis>Linear Models from Graphs</emphasis></para>
      <blockquote>
        <para>For 9 - 12, use the situation and graph below:</para>
        <para>The graph models the cost in dollars, \(C\), of renting a tent at a campground for n nights.
          <figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/dbc7eea714a05aa6c75d90c04a2cc22bd3aae58a"/></media></figure></para>
      </blockquote>
      <para> What is the \(y\)-intercept of the graph? </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 30</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q#10-->
  <exercise data-content-id="04a3607e-460c-4272-bfb0-71b0d83a10b9" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="10">
    <problem>
      <para> What is the slope, or rate of change? </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 10</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
